<h2>Context</h2>
<p>
  <code>fluxb.ps1 Publish</code> could already produce four layouts, but none was designated as the release artifact, and nothing kept the code AOT-compatible between releases. A trial NativeAOT publish for <code>linux-x64</code> on 2026-10-26 found:
</p>
<ul>
  <li>two trim/AOT warnings, both from the generic <code>JsonArray.Add&lt;T&gt;</code> in <code>MediaReport.ToJson</code>. With those fixed, the publish has no warnings even with warnings treated as errors;</li>
  <li>no warnings from Spectre.Console, System.CommandLine, Microsoft.Data.Sqlite, or YamlDotNet (FluxEncoder uses only its event parser and emitter);</li>
  <li>the same runtime behaviour as the JIT build for <code>info</code> in all six formats, <code>encode</code>, <code>--dry-run</code>, <code>merge</code>, <code>history</code>, <code>config</code>, <code>apply</code>, and SIGINT cancellation;</li>
  <li>an 8.8 MB executable plus <code>libe_sqlite3.so</code> (1.5 MB), against roughly 70 MB for a self-contained JIT build;</li>
  <li>a glibc floor of 2.34 for both the executable and the SQLite native library.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Decision</h2>

