<p>
  NativeAOT cannot cross-compile between operating systems, so each OS needs its own runner. Linux builds link against the build host's glibc; the current floor is glibc 2.34 (Debian 12, Ubuntu 22.04, RHEL 9).
</p>

<h2>Consequences</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Reflection fails the build:</strong> reflection-based serialization, <code>Type.GetType</code> lookups, and dynamic code are rejected. Use the non-generic <code>JsonNode</code> APIs, <code>Utf8JsonWriter</code>, or System.Text.Json source generation instead.</li>
  <li><strong>Package upgrades:</strong> a package version that introduces trim warnings cannot be adopted until those warnings are resolved or the package is replaced.</li>
  <li><strong>New RIDs:</strong> add each new RID to <code>RuntimeIdentifiers</code> and regenerate the lock files with <code>dotnet restore --force-evaluate</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Follow-up tasks:</strong> <code>TSKE015.2</code> covers the automated AOT smoke test for each RID, <code>TSKE015.3</code> archive naming, checksums, signatures, and SBOMs, and <code>TSKE015.5</code> the licensing of FFmpeg-bundled archives.</li>
</ul>
